  "mechanismSummary": "Methylmagnesium bromide adds to the carbonyl carbon of ethyl acetate. The tetrahedral intermediate collapses and ethoxide leaves, giving acetone. The ketone is more electrophilic than the ester, so a second methyl adds at once. Acid work-up protonates the alkoxide: tert-butanol.",
